```c
static inline int syscall_get_nr(struct task_struct *task, struct pt_regs *regs)
{
	return regs->orig_ax;
}
```

`regs->orig_ax` is the raw syscall number from userspace. Userspace can set this to **any value** — including values >= NR_syscalls or even negative values (though negative is caught by the `< 0` check).

